end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=13.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":3530,"name":"Roots of Transformed Radical Functions"},"example":{"id":8144,"title":"Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"},"group":{"id":16002,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251516,"answer":{"id":62310583,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:10:14.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11423},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62310589,"created":"2026-10-16T00:10:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12632,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 12:10 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":102416,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":8143,"text":"<p>Find the root of $f(x) = \\sqrt[7]{3x+13} - 1.$</p>\n","choice1":"$x=-4$","choice2":"$x=4$","choice3":"$x=\\dfrac 4 3$","choice4":"$x=-\\dfrac{13}{3}$","choice5":"The function has no roots","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\\[\n\\sqrt[7]{3x+13} - 1 = 0\n\\]</p>\n<p>We solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt[7]{3x+13} - 1 & = 0 \\\\[3pt]\n\\sqrt[7]{3x+13} & = 1 \\\\[3pt]\n\\big(\\sqrt[7]{3x+13}\\big)^7 & = 1^7 \\\\[3pt]\n3x+13 & = 1 \\\\[3pt]\n3x & = -12 \\\\[3pt]\nx & = -4\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-4.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":3530,"name":"Roots of Transformed Radical Functions"},"example":{"id":8143,"title":"Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"},"group":{"id":43389,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251516,"answer":{"id":62310589,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:10:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"se